==Trivia==
*Like [[Sage of Mind Soractes|Soractes]] and [[Sage of Selection Darvin|Darvin]], Sage of Logic Newtone's Japanese name is slightly different from the historical figure he's based on. In Japanese, the real [[wikipedia:Isaac Newton|Newton]] is ニュートン ''Nyūton'', whereas the [[The Battle Cats|Battle Cats]] character is ニュトーン ''Nyutōn''. It may be a pun on ストーン ''sutōn'' (stone), referencing his [[:Category:Sage Enemies|Sage]] stone, or 入湯 ''nyūtō'' (taking a hot bath; bathing in a hot spring), since he's [[:Category:Red Enemies|Red]] and appears underwater.
**His Japanese name and Red trait may also be derived from the [[wikipedia:Philosopher's stone|philosopher's stone]], a legendary alchemical substance usually depicted as a red stone. [[wikipedia:Isaac Newton's occult studies#Alchemical research|Newton spent decades studying alchemy]] and is thought to have been pursuing the philosopher's stone.
**His Slow ability and [[Master of Logic Newtone (Special Cat)|allied self]]'s [[:Category:Floating Enemies|Floating]] target may imply some form of gravity manipulation.
**Because of his Red trait, [[Apple Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Apple Cat]] can ironically be used to freeze Sage of Logic Newtone.
**During his attack animation, the movements made by the spheres that Sage of Logic Newtone holds up mirror the movements made by the swinging spheres of a [[wikipedia:Newton's cradle|Newton's cradle]].
**[[Truth's Devouring Maw]]'s Japanese name, Banbutsu Izanau Shinri no Ōuzu (万物誘う真理の大渦, "Great Whirlpool of Truth That Entices All Things"), may be a reference to the Newton quote "I do not know what I may appear to the world, but to myself I seem to have been only like a boy playing on the sea-shore, and diverting myself in now and then finding a smoother pebble or a prettier shell than ordinary, whilst the <u>great ocean of truth</u> lay all undiscovered before me."
**Sage of Logic Newtone may have been foreshadowed by the name of the sub-chapter preceding Truth's Devouring Maw, [[Newtown Trench]].
*Prior to [[Version 15.4 Update|Version 15.4]], Sage of Logic Newtone lacked the extra ''e'' at the end of his name, matching the real world Newton.
**The change may have been made to add a pun, as Sage of Logic Newtone is Red, in other words a ''new tone''. It may also be a pun on ''stone'' similarly to his Japanese name.
**The change was later reverted in Version 15.4.1, however the name change was reinstated in [[Version 15.5 Update|Version 15.5]].
*According to the Japanese descriptions of Sage of Logic Newtone, Sage of Mind Soractes and Sage of Selction Darvin, the world they are observing is specifically the [[wikipedia:Present life|present life]] (現世 ''gen sei'', ''utsushi yo''), a concept in certain religions such as Shinto and Buddhism.
*Sage of Logic Newtone may have been inspired by Abrahamic religions' story of the [[wikipedia:Garden of Eden|Garden of Eden]], as he was added in the same update as [[Temptation's Rhapsody]], Truth's Devouring Maw's Japanese name can be translated as "Great Whirlpool of Truth That <u>Tempts</u> All Things", he attacks with an apple (the most common depiction of the [[wikipedia:Forbidden fruit|forbidden fruit]]), and eating the fruit gave Adam and Eve forbidden [[:Category:Sage Enemies|knowledge]]. Furthermore, [[Immeasurable Power]] contains [[Angelic Gory]], a fallen [[:Category:Angel Enemies|Angel]], and the serpent that tempted Eve is often associated with [[wikipedia:Samael|Samael]] and Satan, who are fallen angels in many of their depictions.

